@startuml login-success
title Login success: nurse.patel calls GET /api/me with HTTP Basic\n(stateless: no session is created, so every request repeats this whole exchange)
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Client
participant BasicAuthenticationFilter
participant ProviderManager
participant DaoAuthenticationProvider
participant DemoUserDetailsService
participant PasswordEncoder
participant AuthenticationEventPublisher
participant AuthorizationFilter
participant MeController

Client -> BasicAuthenticationFilter : GET /api/me\nAuthorization: Basic base64(nurse.patel:patel-pass)
BasicAuthenticationFilter -> ProviderManager : authenticate(token: "nurse.patel", "patel-pass")
ProviderManager -> DaoAuthenticationProvider : authenticate(token)
DaoAuthenticationProvider -> DemoUserDetailsService : loadUserByUsername("nurse.patel")
DemoUserDetailsService --> DaoAuthenticationProvider : new ClinicUser(ROLE_NURSE, "{bcrypt}$2a$10$...")
DaoAuthenticationProvider -> PasswordEncoder : matches("patel-pass", "{bcrypt}$2a$10$...")\nDelegatingPasswordEncoder: the {bcrypt} prefix selects BCrypt (cost 10, about 70 ms)
PasswordEncoder --> DaoAuthenticationProvider : true
DaoAuthenticationProvider --> ProviderManager : authenticated token (principal: ClinicUser)
ProviderManager -> AuthenticationEventPublisher : publish AuthenticationSuccessEvent\n(delivered to SecurityEventListener, the audit trail)
ProviderManager --> BasicAuthenticationFilter : authenticated token
BasicAuthenticationFilter -> AuthorizationFilter : chain.doFilter(...)\nSecurityContext = nurse.patel, for this request only
AuthorizationFilter -> MeController : rule "authenticated" is met: me(...)
MeController --> Client : 200 OK {"username":"nurse.patel","role":"NURSE",...}

@enduml
